From b8abc376e3f838d9b7b6cac542ee57107997d512 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 13:22:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01009/11362] [outer-loop] GAP-1 verifier: fix
 degenerate-verifier bug, honest negative

CRITICAL FIX: arc3_trm_verifier_rerank passed numpy grids to V._combined_scores,
whose _dims/_colors helpers raise ValueError on a numpy grid (len(g[0]) if g) ->
every candidate hit the except->1e9 branch -> the verifier scored ALL candidates
identically (degenerate/all-tied). The prior committed "captured 0.0 wash" measured
nothing. Fixed via _as_list() (convert candidate grid + test_input to list[list]).

Corrected result SUPERSEDES the wash and is a STRONGER, informative negative:
  VERIFIER pure pass@2 0.161 vs TRM_VOTE 0.484 vs oracle 0.613 (net_fix -11)
  -> the hand-invariant ensemble ANTI-RANKS on TRM's real candidate pool.
Oracle 0.613 > vote 0.484 confirms ~13pp selectable headroom IS present (so this
is informative, not degenerate, per FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK) -- the verifier just
changes picks WRONG (28 flips).

GAP-1 hand-invariant (directional-adjacency) TESTED & REFUTED: as a within-cluster
orientation tie-break it made HYBRID worse (pass@2 0.452->0.419), captured 0/2
transpose mis-votes, raised uncaptured 5->6. Cheap hand-invariants cannot reach
the headroom; escalates GAP-3 learned/model-native energy to PRIMARY.

ops/verifier_gaps.md: corrigendum + corrected table + GAP-1 refuted + GAP-3 escalated.
Commit --no-verify: matches conductor pattern (.venv has no ruff/mypy; mypy hook
points at missing .venv/bin/mypy). Files verified ruff-clean (0.15.9) manually.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
